<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Øresund</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Oresund, the Sound, The Sound, Öresund</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Øresund, or the Sound, is the strait between the Danish island of Zealand and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scania">Scania</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, the main passage between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a>. At its narrowest, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helsingor">Helsingør</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helsingborg">Helsingborg</a>, it is about four kilometres wide. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> levied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sound-toll">Sound Dues</a> on passing ships from 1429 until 1857, a major source of royal revenue.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oresund.jpg" alt="Øresund" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Boeing720 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_%C3%98resund_new_version.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
